% M7-T22 / D-0086 (a): the same root-arm defect as root_nested_defining_gcc_unsat, reached
% through all_different instead of gcc (`bench/fuzz/gen.py ad 25920`, shrunk greedily).
% FIXED; an ordinary passing model test whose proof is verified on every run.
%
% THE DEFECT. The root conflict's derivation cites an all_different [Gone_hole_root]
% cancel -- a [Defining] nested under a [Term] -- and with no root trace on the page it
% minted `rup +1 ~x1_eq_3 >= 1 ;`, which 3.0.2 refused at line 31 ("not implied by
% reverse unit propagation") on the pre-fix binary (sha256 a57f2961...).
%
% THE FIX is search.ml's root arm, which now writes the root trace before any root
% derivation that contains a nested [Defining]. No SAT twin: see root_nested_defining_gcc_unsat.
var 2..4: x0 :: output_var;
var 2..4: x1 :: output_var;
var 2..4: x2 :: output_var;
var 1..1: x3 :: output_var;
var 2..4: x4 :: output_var;
var 1..1: x5 :: output_var;
constraint all_different_int([x5,x0,x2,x1]);
constraint array_int_element(x0,[3,4,1,3],x4);
constraint array_int_element(x2,[3,3,2,3],x4);
constraint int_ne(x4,x1);
solve :: int_search([x1,x0,x3,x2,x5,x4], largest, indomain_median, complete) satisfy;
